; Intro / story-screen kanji escape table.
;
; The intro renderer (code at SNES $85:F010, file $05F010) treats `FE XX`
; as a 2-byte sequence — `XX` is an index into a 256-entry kanji font at
; file $104000 (each glyph = 4 × 16B 2bpp tiles = 64 B). The dialog engine
; ($05:8000) treats FE as a 1-byte pause control, so this table applies
; ONLY to the intro narrative blocks (data/jp/intro.txt) and any other
; section that goes through the bank-$9F renderer.
;
; Identifications below were read off `export/font_tiles/kanji_grid.png`
; (output of `tools/dump_kanji_grid.py`). Several glyphs are visually
; ambiguous between near-identical kanji — flagged with `; ?` where the
; reader was uncertain. Re-render the PNG and verify in-emulator before
; relying on those for translation work.
;
; Generated 2026-05-19. Re-run `tools/dump_kanji_grid.py` after any ROM
; modification to the $104000..$108000 region.

